<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Settings-search index copy. One name (and, where useful, a one-line
  description) per row of the settings information architecture, keyed by the
  row's stable anchor (see SettingEntry.anchorKey()). The settings hub search
  resolves these and feeds them to the pure-domain SettingsSearchEngine.

  Completeness is enforced by SettingsSearchCatalogTest: every registry anchor
  must have a name entry here, so a setting added in the registry cannot silently
  fall out of search.
-->
